+degraded where the day&#39;s background is also low.</p>
+<p><strong>What was built (0.41, D18).</strong> An almanac-HDOP scorer, <code>kshana::interference_map::almanac_hdop</code>, built from
+public material only and labelled as Kshana&#39;s own method; it does not reproduce the paper above. For each report:</p>
+<ul>
+<li>HDOP at the report&#39;s position and time, from the GPS almanac of the day in the YUMA format published by the U.S.
+Coast Guard Navigation Center (<a href="https://www.navcen.uscg.gov/">https://www.navcen.uscg.gov/</a>). Satellites are propagated with the almanac
+equations of IS-GPS-200, with an elevation mask stated by the caller (geodetic horizon).</li>
+<li>The 95 % horizontal bound (EPU) of the report&#39;s NACp category. The table is quoted from J. Sun, <em>The 1090
+Megahertz Riddle</em> (open textbook), Table 1.9.</li>
+<li>A flag when the EPU exceeds a stated multiple of the geometry-predicted 95 % error <code>2 · HDOP · σ_UERE</code>. The
+multiple and <code>σ_UERE</code> are parameters with no default. No value was chosen from real data.</li>
+</ul>
+<p>Its checks (<code>tests/almanac_hdop.rs</code>):</p>
+<ul>
+<li>HDOP equals an independent numpy computation (<code>xval/almanac-hdop/oracle.py</code>) at 20 stated points, to 1.6e-15
+(the requirement was 1e-9).</li>
+<li>The NACp mapping equals the quoted table.</li>
+<li>The flag is exact on 12 hand-written reports.</li>
+</ul>
+<p>The observatory&#39;s products do not use the scorer. Scoring real days with it, for example against the base method,
+is an evidence question with its own pre-registration, committed before that run.</p>
