-        <div class="mp-stage" id="mcpStage"><noscript><div class="crawl-text"><p>A recorded session with the kshana-mcp server (Model Context Protocol, engine v0.40.0): the assistant lists the 52 tools, validates <code>clock-holdover.toml</code> (valid: detected scenario kind `clock`) and runs it: scenario 5ba83a232b94 | quantum holdover 6600s p95 1.20e-4ns integrity 1.000 security n/a (no attack) | classical holdover 2610s p95 19.7ns integrity 1.000 security n/a (no attack).</p><ul><li><code>animate_scenario</code>: Run a Kshana scenario and return its time series as an animation.</li><li><code>assess_receiver_log</code>: Assess a real GNSS receiver log for trust: read a u-blox UBX, RINEX 3 (optionally with broadcast navigation, which adds the engine&#x27;s own fix, RAIM and a clock-aided monitor), Android GnssLogger or NMEA log, run the trust monitors (carrier-to-noise density drop, AGC, jamming indicator, loss of lock, position jump, RAIM, clock) against a calibration baseline, and return when and why the receiver stopped being trustworthy.</li><li><code>assess_vessel_log</code>: Assess a vessel&#x27;s NMEA 0183 log as a batch run (`kshana receiver-trust` with `[platform] kind = &quot;vessel&quot;`): the score model, the monitors that ran and every epoch&#x27;s 0-100 score with its deductions, its satellite geometry (good, degraded, unknown) with a `label` (good, fair, poor) on every epoch, geometry deducting only when poor, and a class on every deduction (geometry, environment, inconsistency), with `geometry_model` (thresholds, the cap and floor in force, and provenance) and `geometry_summary`.</li><li><code>assess_vessel_stream</code>: Score a bounded excerpt of a vessel&#x27;s NMEA 0183 stream the way `kshana receiver-trust live` scores it, and return per-epoch trust state (calibrating, nominal, degraded, untrusted) and 0-100 score with the monitors that deducted (live JSON-lines schema 1.3: each epoch carries `position`, an `advisory` statement that the output is advisory, and its satellite `geometry` (good, degraded with reasons such as few-satellites or high-pdop, or unknown when the excerpt has no GSV or GSA) with a `label` (good, fair, poor; geometry deducts only when poor); every deduction carries a `class`: geometry (the sky, not a finding that no attack occurred), environment or inconsistency (attack-like)), the summary (counts by state, geometry and class, lowest and final score, when the first untrusted epoch came) and the last `$PKSHT` sentence.</li><li><code>attach_evidence_timestamp</code>: Bind an RFC 3161 timestamp token to an evidence pack (`kshana evidence attach-timestamp`), in memory: `files` is a pack as `create_evidence_pack` returns it, `token_base64` the bytes of the `.tsr` file from a timestamp authority.</li><li><code>build_interference_map</code>: Build a GNSS interference map from openly licensed aircraft (ADS-B NIC/NACp) or ship (AIS) position reports given as CSV text (`kshana interference-map adsb|ais`).</li><li><code>compliance_mapping</code>: The static public-framework mapping (`kshana compliance-report --mapping` / `--sources`) as Markdown: one table per framework with each row&#x27;s paraphrased ask, the Kshana outputs that support evidence for it and the gap the outputs do not close; or, with `sources` true, the source documents the tables cite with versions and URLs.</li><li><code>compliance_report</code>: Fill the public-framework mapping from Kshana result documents (`kshana compliance-report`): which rows of six resilience frameworks and standards (the US DHS Resilient PNT framework v2.0, IMO guidance for ships, EASA guidance for aviation, NIS2 Article 21, EN 16803, NIST IR 8323r1) the runs given support evidence for, which they do not, and the gap each row keeps.</li><li><code>connect_map</code>: Map any receiver, timing or monitoring log to Kshana observations with a `kshana.connect/1` mapping file, no code (`kshana connect map`, docs/CONNECT.md).</li><li><code>create_evidence_pack</code>: Create a signed evidence pack for a window of a vessel&#x27;s NMEA 0183 log (`kshana receiver-trust evidence`): the raw log bytes for the window, the configuration with every threshold, the per-epoch results and reasons, a self-contained summary page, and a manifest listing every file&#x27;s SHA-256 with the full log&#x27;s hash and a hash chain, signed with Ed25519.</li><li><code>create_round_trip_pack</code>: Create the signed laboratory round-trip pack (`kshana evidence round-trip`, docs/spec/TEST-CONDITIONS.md): links by hash the scenario that produced the motion, the laboratory&#x27;s `kshana.test-conditions/1` document, the receiver log and its score against the stated events, in a signed evidence pack whose `config.json` carries a `round_trip` block.</li><li><code>export_interop</code>: Export a Kshana scenario in one interoperability format: `czml` (Cesium Language, for CesiumJS), `kml` (Keyhole Markup Language, for Google Earth and geographic information system tools), `geojson` (RFC 7946), `stk` (Systems Tool Kit ephemeris `.e`, one file per satellite) or `sigmf` (Signal Metadata Format recording of a `spectrum` scenario&#x27;s synthesised samples).</li><li><code>export_oem</code>: Export an `orbit` scenario&#x27;s propagated constellation as CCSDS OEM 2.0 ephemeris text — the inertial (TEME) state time series carrying position AND velocity, which flight-dynamics tools (GMAT / Orekit / STK) read.</li><li><code>export_omm</code>: Export an `orbit` scenario&#x27;s mean elements as a CCSDS 502.0-B-2 OMM (Orbit Mean-Elements Message) catalogue — one OMM per satellite.</li><li><code>export_sp3</code>: Export an `orbit` scenario&#x27;s propagated constellation as SP3-c precise-ephemeris text (the standard GNSS post-processing format).</li><li><code>export_table_csv</code>: Run a Kshana scenario and return its reproducibility table as CSV text — the byte-stable table the CLI writes as `&lt;scenario&gt;.table.csv` and the papers cite.</li><li><code>export_test_bench</code>: Export a scenario&#x27;s vehicle motion and events for a laboratory GNSS simulator (`kshana bench-export`, docs/TEST-BENCH.md): a motion CSV and its JSON description (Earth-fixed and geodetic position, velocity, attitude, UTC), NMEA 0183 GGA/RMC sentences, a waypoint text when the sample grid is millisecond-regular, and the scenario&#x27;s events as CSV and as `[[events]]` TOML for a `receiver-trust` scenario.</li><li><code>fit_imu_log</code>: Fit the sensor parameters of the `hybrid` and `fusion` scenarios from a stationary IMU log (`kshana imu-fit`, docs/MACHINE-INPUTS.md).</li><li><code>generate_training_nmea</code>: Generate synthetic bridge NMEA 0183 for crew training from a `nmea-scenario` TOML (`kshana nmea-scenario`): a vessel track and a timeline of scripted events (jamming, position drag-off, time spoof, replay delay, with recovery).</li><li><code>get_example_scenario</code>: Return the TOML text of one bundled reference scenario, byte for byte the file the repository ships under `scenarios/`.</li><li><code>import_route</code>: Write a GeoJSON route into a Kshana scenario that flies a waypoint track, and return the new scenario TOML (run it with run_scenario).</li><li><code>interference_emitter_regions</code>: Estimate emitter regions from openly licensed aircraft (ADS-B) or ship (AIS) reports given as CSV text (`kshana interference-map locate`): where, under stated assumptions, a source of the degraded reports could be, as regions at stated confidence levels with a centroid and an uncertainty ellipse, never a bare point.</li><li><code>iq_acquire</code>: FFT acquisition of one or more PRNs over an IQ recording in the work directory (`kshana iq acquire`).</li><li><code>iq_campaign</code>: Run a lab-replay campaign held in the work directory (`kshana iq campaign`): recordings (each described by a `kshana.test-conditions/1` file stating the lab&#x27;s known truth) x front-end chains x loop designs, each cell tracked and scored against t