e, geometry and class, lowest and final score, when the first untrusted epoch came) and the last `$PKSHT` sentence."},{"name":"attach_evidence_timestamp","does":"Bind an RFC 3161 timestamp token to an evidence pack (`kshana evidence attach-timestamp`), in memory: `files` is a pack as `create_evidence_pack` returns it, `token_base64` the bytes of the `.tsr` file from a timestamp authority."},{"name":"build_interference_map","does":"Build a GNSS interference map from openly licensed aircraft (ADS-B NIC/NACp) or ship (AIS) position reports given as CSV text (`kshana interference-map adsb|ais`)."},{"name":"compliance_mapping","does":"The static public-framework mapping (`kshana compliance-report --mapping` / `--sources`) as Markdown: one table per framework with each row's paraphrased ask, the Kshana outputs that support evidence for it and the gap the outputs do not close; or, with `sources` true, the source documents the tables cite with versions and URLs."},{"name":"compliance_report","does":"Fill the public-framework mapping from Kshana result documents (`kshana compliance-report`): which rows of six resilience frameworks and standards (the US DHS Resilient PNT framework v2.0, IMO guidance for ships, EASA guidance for aviation, NIS2 Article 21, EN 16803, NIST IR 8323r1) the runs given support evidence for, which they do not, and the gap each row keeps."},{"name":"connect_map","does":"Map any receiver, timing or monitoring log to Kshana observations with a `kshana.connect/1` mapping file, no code (`kshana connect map`, docs/CONNECT.md)."},{"name":"create_evidence_pack","does":"Create a signed evidence pack for a window of a vessel's NMEA 0183 log (`kshana receiver-trust evidence`): the raw log bytes for the window, the configuration with every threshold, the per-epoch results and reasons, a self-contained summary page, and a manifest listing every file's SHA-256 with the full log's hash and a hash chain, signed with Ed25519."},{"name":"create_round_trip_pack","does":"Create the signed laboratory round-trip pack (`kshana evidence round-trip`, docs/spec/TEST-CONDITIONS.md): links by hash the scenario that produced the motion, the laboratory's `kshana.test-conditions/1` document, the receiver log and its score against the stated events, in a signed evidence pack whose `config.json` carries a `round_trip` block."},{"name":"export_interop","does":"Export a Kshana scenario in one interoperability format: `czml` (Cesium Language, for CesiumJS), `kml` (Keyhole Markup Language, for Google Earth and geographic information system tools), `geojson` (RFC 7946), `stk` (Systems Tool Kit ephemeris `.e`, one file per satellite) or `sigmf` (Signal Metadata Format recording of a `spectrum` scenario's synthesised samples)."},{"name":"export_oem","does":"Export an `orbit` scenario's propagated constellation as CCSDS OEM 2.0 ephemeris text — the inertial (TEME) state time series carrying position AND velocity, which flight-dynamics tools (GMAT / Orekit / STK) read."},{"name":"export_omm","does":"Export an `orbit` scenario's mean elements as a CCSDS 502.0-B-2 OMM (Orbit Mean-Elements Message) catalogue — one OMM per satellite."},{"name":"export_sp3","does":"Export an `orbit` scenario's propagated constellation as SP3-c precise-ephemeris text (the standard GNSS post-processing format)."},{"name":"export_table_csv","does":"Run a Kshana scenario and return its reproducibility table as CSV text — the byte-stable table the CLI writes as `<scenario>.table.csv` and the papers cite."},{"name":"export_test_bench","does":"Export a scenario's vehicle motion and events for a laboratory GNSS simulator (`kshana bench-export`, docs/TEST-BENCH.md): a motion CSV and its JSON description (Earth-fixed and geodetic position, velocity, attitude, UTC), NMEA 0183 GGA/RMC sentences, a waypoint text when the sample grid is millisecond-regular, and the scenario's events as CSV and as `[[events]]` TOML for a `receiver-trust` scenario."},{"name":"fit_imu_log","does":"Fit the sensor parameters of the `hybrid` and `fusion` scenarios from a stationary IMU log (`kshana imu-fit`, docs/MACHINE-INPUTS.md)."},{"name":"generate_training_nmea","does":"Generate synthetic bridge NMEA 0183 for crew training from a `nmea-scenario` TOML (`kshana nmea-scenario`): a vessel track and a timeline of scripted events (jamming, position drag-off, time spoof, replay delay, with recovery)."},{"name":"get_example_scenario","does":"Return the TOML text of one bundled reference scenario, byte for byte the file the repository ships under `scenarios/`."},{"name":"import_route","does":"Write a GeoJSON route into a Kshana scenario that flies a waypoint track, and return the new scenario TOML (run it with run_scenario)."},{"name":"interference_emitter_regions","does":"Estimate emitter regions from openly licensed aircraft (ADS-B) or ship (AIS) reports given as CSV text (`kshana interference-map locate`): where, under stated assumptions, a source of the degraded reports could be, as regions at stated confidence levels with a centroid and an uncertainty ellipse, never a bare point."},{"name":"iq_acquire","does":"FFT acquisition of one or more PRNs over an IQ recording in the work directory (`kshana iq acquire`)."},{"name":"iq_campaign","does":"Run a lab-replay campaign held in the work directory (`kshana iq campaign`): recordings (each described by a `kshana.test-conditions/1` file stating the lab's known truth) x front-end chains x loop designs, each cell tracked and scored against the stated conditions (time to loss of lock, re-acquisition time, C/N0 degradation against the stated J/S beside an analytic reference labelled MODELLED, false-lock rate, PLL/DLL jitter, availability)."},{"name":"iq_campaign_status","does":"Report a lab-replay campaign's progress from its output folder in the work directory, reading files only: cells done and pending, the recordings, front ends and designs in the plan, and the `digest` once every cell is done."},{"name":"iq_frontend","does":"Apply receiver front-end and interference-mitigation DSP to an IQ recording in the work directory and write the result as a new raw recording with a `<out>.json` sidecar (`kshana iq frontend`)."},{"name":"iq_info","does":"Describe one IQ recording in the work directory without processing it: kind (raw with sidecar, SigMF, SigMF collection), sample format, sample rate, centre frequency, total samples, duration, data files and their size, capture boundaries and annotation count, as JSON (the same row `kshana iq info` prints)."},{"name":"iq_labfit","does":"Fit the tracking-loop loss-of-lock model to lab runs (`kshana iq labfit`): an `iq-labfit` scenario TOML names one or more runs, each a receiver log plus its stated test conditions; the engine loads each log, fits the loop and empirical models, bootstraps the uncertainty and computes the hold-out error."},{"name":"iq_monitor","does":"Run the interference and spoofing detection monitors over an IQ recording in the work directory (`kshana iq monitor`): the wideband `power` and `spectral` monitors, and, given `signal` + `prns`, the per-satellite C/N0 and signal-quality monitors, each against a baseline learned from the first `baseline_s` seconds (or from a settings file)."},{"name":"iq_scene","does":"Generate a multi-satellite GNSS IQ scene into a file in the work directory (`kshana iq scene`)."},{"name":"iq_signals","does":"The GNSS IQ layer's set-up, as JSON: `signals` (the signal names iq_scene, iq_acquire and iq_track accept), `enabled` (whether the IQ file tools are on), `work_dir` (the only folder they read and write; every path argument is relative to it), `max_samples` (the most complex samples one call may generate or process) and, when off, `reason`."},{"name":"iq_sweep","does":"Replay one IQ recording in the work directory across several tracking-loop designs and report each design's steady-state result (`kshana iq sweep`): the designs are every design of a `kshana.loop-design/1` file (`design`), or the product 